On the eighth day of my internship, I started studying 
Linux commands that are used to search for files and 
information. I read the related sections from the Linux 
book and learned about commands such as find, grep, which,
and whereis. I focused on understanding the differences 
between these commands and the situations in which they 
can be useful.

I also learned how grep can be used to search for specific 
text inside files. In addition, I studied the man command, 
which can be used to access the manual pages of Linux commands. 
I found this useful because it allows users to learn more about 
a command directly from the terminal.

I continued practicing these topics while working on the OverTheWire
Bandit challenges. Some of the challenges required finding specific 
files or information, so I tried to apply the commands I had learned 
from the book while solving them.
